@startuml INA700_pi_cycle
' INA700 - one pick and place cycle, end to end
' Author: Suraj Karki
' Course: INA700 - AI-based pick and place
'
' The vision loop runs continuously whether anyone asks for anything or not;
' a cycle does not start the camera, it reads the newest scene the camera
' threads have already produced. That is why the position handed to the
' robot is milliseconds old rather than the result of a fresh capture.

title INA700 - one cycle, from the operator's click to the object in its slot

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam BoxPadding 10
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #555555
  LifeLineBorderColor #999999
  ParticipantBorderColor #333333
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FDF6E8
  ActorBorderColor #333333
}

actor "operator" as OP

box "main thread" #FFFFFF
  participant "TkView" as VIEW
end box

box "always running" #F7F7F7
  participant "CaptureWorker" as CAP
  participant "InferenceWorker\n(VisionPipeline)" as INF
  participant "MappingWorker\n(CoordinateService)" as MAP
end box

box "cycle thread" #FFFFFF
  participant "CycleController" as CYC
  participant "CompositeSelector" as SEL
  participant "RobotCommander" as CMD
end box

participant "ABB controller" as ROB

== the vision loop, running all the time ==

CAP -> CAP : read() at capture_fps
CAP -> INF : Frame (newest only)
INF -> INF : detect, orient, colour,\nre-solve the marker
note right of INF
  prints the inference time on
  every pass, as the course asks
end note
INF -> MAP : Detections, in pixels
MAP -> MAP : pixels to millimetres,\nrz = slot angle - measured angle
MAP -> VIEW : MappedScene, through SharedState

== the operator asks for one object ==

OP -> VIEW : shape + colour,\n"Send pick to robot"
VIEW -> CYC : PickRequest (through the queue)

CYC -> MAP : the newest scene, not a new capture
CYC -> SEL : select(objects, request)
note right of SEL
  allowed shape, inside the sheet,
  confident enough, the shape asked
  for, the colour asked for, then
  nearest to the origin first
end note
SEL --> CYC : the chosen object

alt nothing matched
  CYC -> VIEW : "no object matched the request"
  note right of CYC
    the attempt is spent; up to three
    in all, a pause between each
  end note
else one was chosen
  CYC -> VIEW : "PRESS THE YELLOW BUTTON"
  CYC -> CMD : send this object
  CMD -> ROB : move <shape> x y rz#

  ROB -> ROB : waits for the yellow button
  OP -> ROB : presses it
  ROB -> ROB : pick at (x, y), rotate by rz,\nplace in that shape's slot
  ROB --> CMD : DONE:

  CMD --> CYC : SUCCESS
  CYC -> VIEW : "the robot is placing the square"

  CYC -> MAP : look again
  alt the object is gone from where it was
    CYC -> VIEW : placed successfully
  else it is still on the board
    CYC -> CYC : retry, the camera disagreed\nwith the robot
  end
end

@enduml
